      "problem": "Given that $X∼U\\{13,14,18\\},$ compute $P(X=14).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{13,14,18\\},$ and the set $S=\\{13,14,18\\}$ has $|S|=3$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & x=13,14,18 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=14)=f(14)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$",
